description: Library-first policy - use the installed stack instead of reimplementing it
alwaysApply: true
---

# Library First

This project picked its stack deliberately. Reimplementing something a dependency
already provides is a defect, not a shortcut. Before writing any component,
hook, or utility, check whether it already exists.

| Need | Use | Never hand-write |
|---|---|---|
| UI primitive | `npx shadcn@latest add <name>` | dialog, select, dropdown, table, toast, tooltip |
| Styling | Tailwind utility classes | CSS modules, styled-components, inline `style={{}}` |
| Forms | `react-hook-form` + `zodResolver` | `useState` per field, manual validation, custom onChange wiring |
| Validation and types | one `zod` schema in `src/shared`, types via `z.infer` | type guards, duplicated interfaces, ad-hoc runtime checks |
| Common hooks | `usehooks-ts` | debounce, localStorage, click-outside, media-query, copy-to-clipboard |
| Collection / object work | `lodash` | bespoke `reduce` chains for grouping, keying, deduping, deep cloning |
| Database access | Drizzle query builder | raw SQL strings |

## Import individual members, never a namespace

```ts
// BAD - pulls the whole library, defeats tree-shaking
import _ from 'lodash'
_.groupBy(rows, 'status')

// GOOD
import { groupBy } from 'lodash'
groupBy(rows, 'status')
```

## Keep it DRY

If the same logic appears twice, extract it. Shared validation belongs in
`src/shared`, shared UI in `src/renderer/src/components`, shared hooks in
`src/renderer/src/hooks`.

## Escalation

Native language features are fine for trivial work: `map`, `filter`, and
`Object.entries` do not need lodash. But if a real requirement genuinely is not
covered by the stack, say so explicitly and explain why before writing a bespoke
implementation. Do not silently roll your own.
